<title>BELGIUM: Belgian money market supply raised in week.</title>
<headline>Belgian money market supply raised in week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian central bank said it added liquidity to the money market in the week to March 28 to offset a rise in notes in circulation.</p>
<p>(figures from the weekly statement in bln francs) -</p>
<p> Foreign currency reserves	   450.457 ( + 0.796)</p>
<p> Advances against pledged security   8.695 ( - 7.322)</p>
<p> Commercial bills			  2.638 ( - 0.029)</p>
<p> Securities portfolio		   23.815 ( - 0.002)</p>
<p> Money market interventions*	 107.578 ( + 8.645)</p>
<p> Bank notes in circulation	   462.216 ( + 4.653)</p>
<p>* comprises repurchase agreements and interbank loans</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
